60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option D has an engineering team present. That helps with the admin gap.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, D is built for transport. It might handle our yard devices better.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, but D is on our servers. We have no staff to maintain it.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, B has a regional service team. That solves the support ownership issue.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, B is hosted. That avoids the upgrade hell we saw with the dispatch tool.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, but B is a fixed configuration. Our rules change often.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, C has configurable workflows. But the partner firm is risky.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, C is a subscription. That is a recurring operating cost. The board likes that.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, but C uses a partner for training. We saw that fail in 2018.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, true. The data lift was a disaster. We need internal control.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,D's team stays through rollout. That is the only one that addresses the people gap.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I agree. The yard needs a system that fits our reality, not a cloud dream.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I am worried about the maintenance cost of D. But the other options have hidden risks.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,B's support team is a single point of contact. That is what I need.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,D is the only one that doesn't rely on external partners for critical tasks.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for D. The engineering team is essential.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I vote for D. It fits our yard and calendar.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for B. The hosted model avoids the maintenance trap.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for B. The regional support team is reliable.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for D. We cannot trust external partners with our data again.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
